WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.080
It just started.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:07.040
Yep, looks like that worked. Good job.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.880
Amanda can get back in at some point anyway.

00:00:16.145 --> 00:00:20.465
>> All right, so again, just want to thank everybody for joining us this afternoon.

00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:22.705
So I said it's

00:00:23.985 --> 00:00:26.785
not particularly where we want to be on a beautiful

00:00:27.105 --> 00:00:31.070
summer like Sunday, but here we are. This is all part of the process.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.710
Just a couple things before we

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.670
move on to the

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.070
agenda for the meeting.

00:00:43.055 --> 00:00:46.015
I think everybody here understands the process.

00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:47.695
Just about everybody who's

00:00:47.775 --> 00:00:51.295
in this meeting has probably followed along at least to some extent.

00:00:52.175 --> 00:00:58.700
Just to reiterate what our job is here is we presented a recommended budget

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.540
to the to

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.660
be reviewed in the town budget meeting.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.260
That budget was passed without any changes.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.980
It then went to referendum

00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:13.745
and was voted down at referendum and per charter,

00:01:13.985 --> 00:01:21.505
it's up to the Board of Finance to review the budget and present either the same or a revised budget to the town

00:01:21.665 --> 00:01:22.865
at the next

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.030
town budget meeting, another town budget meeting, which has been scheduled for Tuesday,

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:30.630
May 25.

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:32.870
If the

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.710
meeting then passes a budget,

00:01:37.415 --> 00:01:43.895
and it'll go on to referendum if we agree on a budget there and do this again. So that's

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:44.695
the process.

00:01:45.255 --> 00:01:46.455
Also, a reminder,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:58.230
there are certain parts of this. I'm not going to go through the entire budget. I think we've all seen it. If you haven't, it's been posted on the website for quite some time.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:00.310
It's been covered in many meetings.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.510
One part of the budget that is not

00:02:05.585 --> 00:02:09.425
up for any debate or change at this point is the RAM budget.

00:02:09.905 --> 00:02:12.305
That is handled through a separate referendum.

00:02:13.345 --> 00:02:14.625
During that referendum,

00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:20.550
it has passed, so there is zero value in my opinion in discussing the RAM budget today.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.710
I would also ask that during the public speak

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.750
sessions,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.150
we've got a lot of people in their attendance today who have already participated

00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:32.005
in the meetings.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.565
I think we pretty much know

00:02:34.805 --> 00:02:36.565
a lot of people's positions.

00:02:37.125 --> 00:02:43.605
I think more to the point is we know what the town's position was in the last budget. It failed pretty significant

00:02:44.245 --> 00:02:44.645
margin.

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.610
We'll just say that.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:53.450
And so what I would ask is that we, in the interest of moving this meeting along,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.810
that if you have specific additions or new information

00:02:58.065 --> 00:03:02.545
that can be presented or should be presented to the Board of Finance, is relevant,

00:03:02.545 --> 00:03:03.745
then we

00:03:03.905 --> 00:03:14.610
welcome your opportunity and welcome your input in either of the public speak sessions on the agenda. I would ask that you not restate things that have already been stated

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.130
previously.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:19.970
Again, I think we all kind of understand what everybody's position is.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:24.210
If you have something new or you've changed your mind or

00:03:24.995 --> 00:03:33.155
that, and we absolutely welcome your input. But I would ask in the interest of moving this along for all involved that we do try to keep this to a

00:03:34.515 --> 00:03:46.170
fairly targeted discussion and keep on new information. We've got a lot of work to do potentially. I'm hoping this isn't a long meeting, but it may be, and there's this just all part of the process. We got a lot to do.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:55.415
Okay, that being said, I'm going to move on to item. I'm also going to state too that we generally try to keep to a three minute time limit, and I don't always enforce that.

00:03:56.375 --> 00:04:01.495
What that means is that you'll be given up to three minutes to talk. I do want you to keep to that limit.

00:04:01.815 --> 00:04:08.670
If everyone's spoken and you have more to say, we can come back around to you. We're not going to stop your ability to

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.310
speak at the meeting,

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:13.950
especially particularly if you have something

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.550
that you want to add. But I do want to keep to that limit. I'm not sure that there's much value in going beyond that,

00:04:20.285 --> 00:04:23.805
but we want to make sure that everybody has a chance to speak and that we

00:04:25.165 --> 00:04:27.245
move this meeting along efficiently.

00:04:28.445 --> 00:04:32.845
Okay, that being said, let's go on to agenda item number two, which is our public speak.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.290
Amanda, do you want to go around and see if who's got input if anyone?

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.010
>> Sure thing. Okay, first up for public speak is Scott Persson.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:47.130
>> I'm all set, Amanda. Thank you for asking. Thanks, Scott.

00:04:49.195 --> 00:04:50.475
Jerry Cremay.

00:04:53.515 --> 00:04:54.635
You're muted.

00:04:58.795 --> 00:04:59.755
>> Thank you.

00:05:00.235 --> 00:05:02.395
I would like to participate if that's okay.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:09.400
I come before you today as a fellow resident taxpayer and a senior citizen on a fixed income.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.720
I wanna thank the board of finance for giving up this Sunday afternoon

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.040
to come together to work on Andover's budget.

00:05:16.635 --> 00:05:19.915
As town residents, we must change the way we think about the budget.

00:05:20.395 --> 00:05:25.595
Realistically, we cannot expect the taxes will stay the same amount year after year.

00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:27.755
Everything goes up in price.

00:05:28.075 --> 00:05:30.075
As a town, Andover's a great community.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.240
We've all made the choice to make this place our home.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.960
As you discuss and deliberate the budget, please keep in mind that it is counterproductive

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:41.240
to pit one segment of the town against the other two segments.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.400
Senior citizens are important.

00:05:44.195 --> 00:05:46.995
We want them to be able to grow old while staying in Andover.

00:05:47.635 --> 00:05:52.115
Our senior citizens need and deserve a community center for which they have been waiting for many years

00:05:52.355 --> 00:05:53.395
even decades.

00:05:53.715 --> 00:05:55.955
We'll serve as a place for them to socialize

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.570
and share a meal.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:04.930
Let's not pit the seniors against the school and the town and create competition for tax dollars. Children are important.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.530
Andover Elementary School is an extremely valuable asset to this town.

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:27.420
Parents of school children will be the first to tell you that AES is a school that cares about this town's youngest residents and it provides children with the best that education has to offer. Our school building and grounds are kept in pristine condition. Let's not put our school district in competition with the town and the seniors for support of tax dollars.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.860
Finally, our town's infrastructure is important. We must support the budget of the board of selectmen.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:43.985
We must take responsibility for fixing roads, bridges, culverts and removal of dead trees. We have to provide public works department with the trucks and equipment they need as well as our volunteer fire department.

00:06:44.305 --> 00:06:46.945
We must provide the employees of the town hall.

00:06:47.505 --> 00:06:52.740
We must not place our town's budget in competition with the AES school district budget and our seniors.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.820
The solution to this problem,

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.620
work together in a respectful kind manner.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:08.325
And any tax dollars spent for the town's board of education, school budget, the board of selectman's town budget, or the senior citizens community center is money well spent.

00:07:08.725 --> 00:07:14.325
Benefit all residents of Andover. Let's make Andover the envy of all small towns in Connecticut.

00:07:14.645 --> 00:07:14.965
Thank you.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.310
Thank you. Thank you, Jerry. Next

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.430
up Valerie Bruno.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.070
You're muted. Are you all set?

00:07:28.895 --> 00:07:30.975
I'm okay on this end. Have shared Okay,

00:07:31.775 --> 00:07:32.575
thank you.

00:07:33.215 --> 00:07:34.815
Next up, Joanne Hubert.

00:07:38.975 --> 00:07:40.095
>> Thanks Amanda.

00:07:40.815 --> 00:07:51.920
I'll be brief Mark. I think it's important. I know we've all stated our things before, but it's important since we're all taking time out of our busy Sunday to be here that we do get a couple minutes just to

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:56.480
address things. I just wanted to say that since the budget has failed,

00:07:56.885 --> 00:07:58.885
the townspeople have spoken,

00:07:59.125 --> 00:08:03.045
and I know all of you currently elected Board of Finance members

00:08:03.525 --> 00:08:09.925
wanted to be on that seat. So now it's time for you guys to do the hard job, and I wish you luck. I won't join you till July,

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:16.260
I just have a couple things to say. So it's clear that we can't afford the 6.7%

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.860
taxation increase.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:34.865
These are true numbers due to the loss of revenue that we know is going to happen with the surplus amount going down, and the taxpayers can't bear that amount. So also, it's been clear from the beginning that you've asked the Board of Ed already to supply some scenarios.

00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:42.220
And I've called it a strategy in the past, and a strategy isn't a bad word at all. I use strategies all the time. So

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:53.980
they're continuously not giving you anything to work with. So today's the day you've got to take the hard line, come in at a zero increase for them. They can do it. The declining enrollment

00:08:53.625 --> 00:08:59.145
can withstand it. If they don't want to give up teachers, they don't have to have them find the money somewhere else.

00:08:59.785 --> 00:09:13.680
Again, when I get on that board, I'm not going to waste my time. I'm going to just come up with things. Want to hear from everybody. I want all of you to have input today. Then lastly, I want to address any parents that are out there. This is quick. Money does not equate education.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:25.825
Please know that you partner with your children. I work in a school. Three of my kids have had 20 to 25 kids in their classrooms. If you send them to school with great manners,

00:09:25.985 --> 00:09:27.745
being respectful of their teachers,

00:09:27.905 --> 00:09:39.920
doing a good job, those teachers will teach your children. They will do a great job. So money does not equate. You start at home as a parent raising model citizens and sending them to school. Thank you.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.120
Good luck.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.520
Thank

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.600
>> you, Joanne. Thanks, Joanne.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:49.755
Next up, Kathy Palazzi and Mike Palazzi.

00:09:53.995 --> 00:09:55.515
We're fine, thank you.

00:09:57.755 --> 00:09:58.715
Thank you.

00:10:00.715 --> 00:10:01.595
Chris Bernard.

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:07.160
>> Good afternoon. Thanks. I will certainly try to keep this as short as possible.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:15.720
So first, I am a member of the board of education. I wanna start off by speaking as a citizen of the community though, and a relatively new one having only been here for about two years now.

00:10:16.855 --> 00:10:19.895
I do fully support the end of our budget,

00:10:20.375 --> 00:10:26.295
having come from another area which had relatively high taxes. I think the taxes are in line for what we're trying to do.

00:10:26.935 --> 00:10:37.310
It is imperative that we have a quality school as it directs not only our families and our students who are currently here, but also as we have seen from some of the Facebook comments, those who chose to move here.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:42.030
But it also has a direct effect upon our property values

00:10:42.435 --> 00:10:43.475
long term.

00:10:43.715 --> 00:10:54.355
I have family of friends with young children who have seen the impact of not having their children in school over the past year. And I think the fact that Andover elementary maintained

00:10:54.355 --> 00:10:57.395
an in person operation throughout the year

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.660
demonstrates not only the staff members

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:05.780
and teachers commitment, but the administrative commitment to doing this in a well thought out manner.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:18.595
And I keep hearing complaints from the town about budgets being impacted because we've not maintained roads or culverts, trees and stuff like that. And I get it, and I understand that and that's past decisions that have been made.

00:11:19.555 --> 00:11:21.715
But if we don't properly fund the schools,

00:11:22.115 --> 00:11:23.475
then we absolutely

00:11:23.715 --> 00:11:25.075
will impact our students.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:36.550
And, I certainly respect Joanne's comment, but I do disagree that money does occasionally lead to better students because that means we can hire and retain proper

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:37.910
teachers in the organization.

00:11:38.635 --> 00:11:41.355
It has been just demonstrated time and time again,

00:11:42.395 --> 00:11:47.435
that if we do not provide the proper commitment to our students when they're young in research,

00:11:47.915 --> 00:11:51.675
that there is after effects. And you

00:11:51.995 --> 00:11:53.675
have myself, I'm doctor of education.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:12:03.570
I know exactly, I've done research, I've done this. We have Valerie, she is very adept at what she does and always takes the students in consideration.

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:09.730
Now flipping over to my board of education hat. And this is speaking of me as a board of education member.

00:12:10.265 --> 00:12:23.385
I feel we have put forth a very responsible budget that is in the best interest of AES students. And I think that's the challenge. We've all put forth budgets that we think is in the best interest of our respective constituencies that we are trying to serve.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:32.580
All of our working sessions and board meetings have had an opportunity for public comment yet with a few exceptions and Joanne has absolutely

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:35.700
joined our meetings and provide her comments and very welcome comments.

00:12:36.455 --> 00:12:43.335
We haven't heard from anybody else in the community for the most part at those meetings about the conversations and the concerns there are.

00:12:44.295 --> 00:12:45.815
Again,

00:12:45.815 --> 00:12:51.495
AES administration staff had done a phenomenal job in acquiring additional grants and monies to help support the schools.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:13:00.950
If the decision is made to cut the AES budget, I as a board member, we'll make the commitment that we will try to make it work as best as possible

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:04.070
without impacting the students and or the families.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:04.630
However,

00:13:05.145 --> 00:13:08.665
we have looked at the budget pretty closely and very carefully,

00:13:08.825 --> 00:13:14.585
and I'm not sure there's a place that we can make an adjustment without affecting the students and or the families.

00:13:15.865 --> 00:13:17.545
And so with that, I thank the board

00:13:17.865 --> 00:13:23.080
and I wish everybody the best of luck. I know this is a tough decision and going forward and

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:28.760
we're here to help. I second Jerry's comments that we all need to work together proactively.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:34.760
And I'm not really sure having been with me for two years, I have seen that. And so I'm looking forward to changing

00:13:34.575 --> 00:13:35.615
that way of

00:13:36.335 --> 00:13:38.255
working together. Thanks.

00:13:40.015 --> 00:13:41.055
Thanks, Chris.

00:13:41.775 --> 00:13:42.815
>> Thank you.

00:13:44.975 --> 00:13:46.015
Kimberly Person.

00:13:47.670 --> 00:13:50.950
Nothing at this time. Thank you, Amanda. Thank you.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.110
Celeste Willard.

00:13:56.870 --> 00:13:58.550
>> Thanks, Amanda. I

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:00.390
just would like to echo

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:02.070
my fellow Board of Education

00:14:03.085 --> 00:14:04.365
members comments.

00:14:04.685 --> 00:14:08.045
I think Chris and Jerry did a excellent

00:14:08.205 --> 00:14:09.165
job in

00:14:11.005 --> 00:14:13.885
putting forth the goals of our board.

00:14:14.285 --> 00:14:14.845
And

00:14:15.565 --> 00:14:16.605
also that

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:17.910
unfortunately,

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:20.310
there's a lot of divide in the town.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.150
And I think Jerry

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:36.465
really kind of hit the nail on the head when he said, you know, we don't want to, you know, pin the seniors against the students and the students against the seniors, because that that's not that that's not a way to run the town that that's not a way to, you

00:14:37.105 --> 00:14:38.385
know, to interact

00:14:38.385 --> 00:14:39.425
in the town.

00:14:39.825 --> 00:14:41.585
And it's it's not a

00:14:42.705 --> 00:14:45.665
there you shouldn't have to choose it should be

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:49.210
not so much of a divide. And unfortunately,

00:14:49.210 --> 00:14:57.130
with Facebook and the comments and the back and forth, I just think it's really kind of unfortunately gotten out of control and there's a lot of misinformation

00:14:57.130 --> 00:15:12.865
out there. So I really want to thank the Board of Finance for doing a wonderful job. I think we finally have some boards in town where people are willing to roll up their sleeves and do the work. And I'm proud to be on the Board of Education and

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:18.370
whatever we need to do to get this budget passed, we will. So thank you.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:23.250
Thank you. Thank you, Celeste.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.330
Liz Lokic.

00:15:28.885 --> 00:15:29.765
>> Hi.

00:15:30.885 --> 00:15:32.245
I don't have anything to

00:15:32.565 --> 00:15:36.085
say publicly. I've sent my comments to the board.

00:15:36.645 --> 00:15:39.685
Thank you. Thank you for being here. Thank

00:15:39.685 --> 00:15:40.885
you. Thank you for all you do.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.420
Thanks, Liz.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.900
Adrian Mandeville.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:49.780
>> Yeah, thanks.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:55.940
Know, I have to say, you know, I do appreciate the Board of Finance putting in the time.

00:15:58.775 --> 00:15:59.415
I

00:15:59.975 --> 00:16:01.335
speaking as a

00:16:01.815 --> 00:16:04.055
individual not as a selectman

00:16:04.535 --> 00:16:05.655
will say that

00:16:05.975 --> 00:16:07.095
you know I

00:16:08.215 --> 00:16:09.335
look at this

00:16:10.055 --> 00:16:10.295
and

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:14.020
I'm a little frustrated, I feel like

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:17.300
we're pitting,

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:23.220
you know, we are pitting one side against the other. And that's, that's hard to, it's hard to deal with.

00:16:24.265 --> 00:16:29.785
You know, I have friends on both sides of this. And we, you know, I got a ton of phone calls this week.

00:16:31.145 --> 00:16:33.385
You know, people that were frustrated on both sides.

00:16:34.025 --> 00:16:35.625
But the one thing I will say,

00:16:36.585 --> 00:16:40.400
you know, I appreciate the Board of Education's efforts, I do.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:44.320
But I think they missed an opportunity at the last meeting on the twelfth.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.720
You know, they realized they had 138,000

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:49.200
leftover.

00:16:50.075 --> 00:16:50.715
And

00:16:51.355 --> 00:16:54.555
instead of looking at what they could return to the town,

00:16:55.035 --> 00:16:56.395
as even Ram did,

00:16:57.995 --> 00:16:59.515
they decided to spend it.

00:17:00.075 --> 00:17:01.995
And they decided to stockpile,

00:17:02.315 --> 00:17:03.835
you know, dollars 54,000

00:17:03.835 --> 00:17:04.475
in grants

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.440
that don't have an expiration date on it.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:08.560
And then

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:11.120
spend down to their 2% cap

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:15.200
that they can keep if the Board of Finance approves at the end of this budget cycle.

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:24.365
And I think that's frustrating. So they had grant money put aside for something and they decided to use budget dollars instead so they can hold the grants for later.

00:17:24.845 --> 00:17:25.725
And

00:17:26.205 --> 00:17:28.445
we're not talking about education

00:17:29.085 --> 00:17:36.720
in an abstract. We don't live vacuum. And so when we start talking about value of education, we're not talking about a teacher,

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.120
we're talking about an outside classroom.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:41.520
It's not

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:43.360
a need.

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:45.120
It's a want.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:49.325
And I think that's the problem is that, you know, on the town side,

00:17:49.485 --> 00:17:55.485
we all see the needs, we see the roads, the bridges, the culprits on and on. And on the school side, we see the needs, we see,

00:17:55.885 --> 00:17:57.885
you know, we see the need for teachers,

00:17:57.885 --> 00:18:00.525
and we see the need for, you know, educational materials.

00:18:01.090 --> 00:18:06.290
But sometimes it's those those wants that creep into the budget that are an issue.

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:11.970
And I think that's the frustration I think a lot of residents, myself included,

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:12.770
